  "name": "OVARIAN ANTIBODY-AOA",
  "code": "2036",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Anti ovarian antibodies are typically found in women with premature ovarian failure. Large numbers of women with unexplained infertility also have anti ovarian antibodies in their blood. Anti ovarian antibodies in them are associated with poor implantation,Anti ovarian antibodies are also found in people with Addison's Disease, thyroid disease and endometriosis.</p>\n<p><strong>Limitation :</strong></p>\n<p>Anti ovarian antibodies are often found in small amounts throughout the general population. About 30% of normal, healthy women have the antibody. However, anti ovarian antibodies are found in very small amounts in these groups and do not interfere with ovarian function.</p>\n<p><strong>Technique:</strong></p>\n<p>BIOCHIP slide with frozen sections of primate ovary covering the reaction areas are used. Indirect<br>Immunofluorescence.</p>",
